body:
Hi,

Following #1027, #1031 and #1106, I am still a bit unclear about what is the recommended / future-proof way of configuring the helper, for setting the distinct parameter in particular. At the moment, the helper is exposed to me in two places :
### Custom searchFunction

``` javascript
var search = instantsearch({
 [...]
  searchFunction: search_func
});

function search_func(helper) {  
  // does not work, distinct is not set in the query
  // helper.setQueryParameter('distinct', 3).search();
}
```
### Custom widget

``` javascript
search.addWidget({
  init: function(args) {
    args.helper.setQueryParameter('distinct', 3);
  }
});
```

I had to resort to using option 2 (custom widget) but as @pixelastic pointed out 

> I would rather keep the widgets for everything that is DOM/UI related

Could you please let me know if the custom widget is the way to go as of now for this kind of customizations?

Thanks!

comments.body:
@mlbrgl If you want to set distinct statically then you can use this:

``` js
var search = instantsearch({
  searchParameters: {
    distinct: 3
  }
});
```

This should be sufficient.

It appears `distinct` does not work in this setup.. I am receiving 10 of the same results.

```
this.search = instantsearch({
searchParameters: {
        hitsPerPage: this.hitsPerPage,
        filters: `_tags:"${this.tagId}"`,
        distinct: true,
        facetingAfterDistinct: true
      },
});
```

Am I missing something?
